---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { BarChart } from "astro-ink";

const signups = [
  { label: "Jan", value: 40 },
  { label: "Feb", value: 55 },
  { label: "Mar", value: 48 },
  { label: "Apr", value: 70 },
  { label: "May", value: 92 },
];

const revenue = [
  { label: "Q1", value: 120 },
  { label: "Q2", value: 180 },
  { label: "Q3", value: 150 },
  { label: "Q4", value: 210 },
];
---
<Base title="BarChart">
  <div class="docs-page">
    <h1>BarChart</h1>
    <p class="docs-lede">
      Vertical bars for your points. Monthly signups below are honest sample
      data, rendered as a static SVG with no tooltips. Only the vertical
      orientation is supported.
    </p>

    <h2>Monthly signups</h2>
    <div class="docs-example">
      <span class="docs-example-label" aria-hidden="true">Monthly signups</span>
      <BarChart data={signups} />
    </div>
    <pre class="docs-code"><code>&lt;BarChart data=&#123;signups&#125; /&gt;</code></pre>

    <h2>With values</h2>
    <p>Pass <code>showValues</code> to print each value above its bar.</p>
    <div class="docs-example">
      <BarChart label="Quarterly revenue" data={revenue} showValues />
    </div>
    <pre class="docs-code"><code>&lt;BarChart label="Quarterly revenue" data=&#123;revenue&#125; showValues /&gt;</code></pre>

    <h2>Props</h2>
    <table class="docs-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>data</code></td><td><code>Array&lt;&#123; label: string; value: number &#125;&gt;</code></td><td>-</td><td>Bars in order, left to right.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>width</code></td><td><code>number</code></td><td><code>560</code></td><td>viewBox width; the SVG scales to <code>100%</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>height</code></td><td><code>number</code></td><td><code>240</code></td><td>viewBox height.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>label</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>"Bar chart"</code></td><td>Chart name; opens the auto-summary.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>showValues</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Print each value above its bar.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>layout</code></td><td><code>"vertical"</code></td><td><code>"vertical"</code></td><td>Only orientation; vertical bars.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>class</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>-</td><td>Style passthrough.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Static honesty</h2>
    <p>
      Static SVG, no tooltips; values appear in text only when
      <code>showValues</code> is set. Bars darken on hover via CSS only. X
      labels longer than 8 characters are truncated with the full text kept in
      a <code>&lt;title&gt;</code>. A zero baseline is clamped into the
      viewBox, so negative values (not shown in the demos) draw below it.
    </p>

    <h2>Accessibility</h2>
    <ul class="docs-list">
      <li>The chart is an image (<code>role="img"</code>) with an auto-summary label: <code>"&#123;Label&#125;, &#123;n&#125; points, high &#123;maxLabel&#125; &#123;max&#125;, low &#123;minLabel&#125; &#123;min&#125;"</code>.</li>
      <li>A <code>&lt;title&gt;</code> repeats the summary and a <code>&lt;desc&gt;</code> describes the reading order.</li>
      <li>Every bar carries a <code>&lt;title&gt;</code> with its <code>"&#123;label&#125;: &#123;value&#125;"</code>.</li>
      <li>Y ticks come from <code>niceTicks</code>; tick and axis text uses the muted token at xs size.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Base>
